{number: 27}
{title: O Come, All Ye Faithful}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] O come, all ye [G] faithful, [C] joyful and tri-[G] umphant,
O [Am] come ye, O [G] come ye to [D7] Beth-[G] lehem;
[C] Come and be-[F] hold [C] Him [Dm] born the [G] King of [Am] an-[G] gels;
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [C] come, let us adore Him,
O [C] come, let us a-[G] dore Him,
O [F] come, let us a-[G] dore [C] Him,
[F] Christ [G] the [C] Lord.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Sing, choirs of [G] angels, [C] sing in exul-[G] tation,
O [Am] sing, all ye [G] bright hosts of [D7] heav'n a-[G] bove;
[C] Glory to [F] God, [C] all [Dm] glory [G] in the [Am] high-[G] est;
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Yea, Lord, we [G] greet Thee, [C] born this happy [G] morning,
[Am] Jesus, to [G] Thee be all [D7] glory [G] giv'n;
[C] Word of the [F] Fa-[C] ther, [Dm] now in [G] flesh ap-[Am] pear-[G] ing;
{end_of_verse}
